# Open on his PC (ISZE)

Jerome opens files on **this** Windows clone. Chat markdown does not launch HTML.

## Hard lines

- Never give `/workspace/...` or `\workspace\...` as something he should run on Windows.
- Never `file://` markdown.
- Never a GitHub `blob/...html` as “open the paper” (private repo 404s while signed out; source view is not the pack).
- Quoted Windows path only under `C:\Users\jerom\Desktop\claude\ISZE\...` and only if that file **exists on this machine**.
- If this session cannot `start` the file on Windows, say so in one sentence. Do not lead with “pull the repo.” If the file lives only on another clone, say that plainly.
- Sibling `OPEN_*.cmd` must be **CRLF**. He double-clicks it in Explorer.

Project hook (this repo): `.cursor/hooks/block-workspace-open-paths.mjs` via `.cursor/hooks.json`. Do **not** dump this into `~\.cursor\hooks`.

See also `isze-html-openable.mdc`.
